  - language: 10
    solidName: Octahedron
    solidFamily: Platonic Solid
    description: A dual pyramid structure formed by eight triangles that naturally
      emerges in high-pressure mineral formations.
    fact1: Two square pyramids joined at their bases.
    fact2: Same number of edges as the cube (12) which is a consequence of duality.
    fact3: If sliced through its center parallel to a face, you get a regular hexagonal
      cross section
    natureEntries:
    - title: Fluorite crystals
      description: Calcium fluoride naturally cleaves into perfect octahedral shapes.
      category: 0
    - title: Diamond rough
      description: Raw diamonds often form octahedral crystals before cutting.
      category: 0
    - title: Molecular geometry
      description: Many transition metal complexes adopt octahedral coordination
        geometry.
      category: 2
